    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u explain what exactly the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? i'm looking at a contract for electronic components moving from korea to germany and need to be sure about the insurance and freight handover points.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the cost of transporting goods to the named port of destination, loading onto the vessel, obtaining marine insurance for the carriage to the port of destination, and covering all transportation costs incurred up to the port of destination. However, the risk of loss or damage to the goods transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods pass the ship's rail at the port of shipment. Thus, while the seller must arrange and pay for insurance and freight, once the goods are delivered to the port of destination, any loss or damage incurred beyond this point becomes the buyer's responsibility.",
      "source": "target",
